  "measures": [
    {
      "name": "Public Measure TX",
      "jurisdiction": "Tama County",
      "ballotLanguage": "Proposition by the eligible electors of Tama County to decrease the number of supervisors to three. Shall the Following Public Measure be adopted? Public Measure TX The number of Tama County Supervisors shall be decreased from five members to three members."
    },
    {
      "name": "Kirkwood Community College Public Measure NC",
      "jurisdiction": "Kirkwood Community College (Merged Area X) - Tama County portion",
      "ballotLanguage": "Shall Kirkwood Community College (Merged Area X) in the Counties of Benton, Black Hawk, Buchanan, Cedar, Clinton, Delaware, Dubuque, Iowa, Jackson, Jefferson, Johnson, Jones, Keokuk, Linn, Louisa, Poweshiek, Tama, and Washington, be authorized to renovate, improve, erect, and equip facilities to modernize learning spaces with an emphasis on health sciences, industrial technologies, agricultural sciences, and business and information technology, contract indebtedness therefor, and issue General Obligation Bonds in an amount not exceeding $88,000,000 for those purposes?"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Names copied from the official sample ballot (differ slightly from candidate list in some cases, e.g. Brett T. Miller vs Brett Thompson Miller). Supervisors elected BY DISTRICT: District 2 and District 3 seats on the 2026 ballot; each appears only on ballot styles in that district (combined 88-page sample ballot PDF: District 2 on 3 styles, District 3 on 7 styles; other styles have no supervisor race). Soil and Water Conservation District Commissioner (vote for two) has no printed candidates (write-in only). Township trustee/clerk are vote-for-one; Clark, Geneseo, Highland, Howard, Tama Twp trustee and Grant, Highland Twp clerk have no candidate. Public Measure TX (reduce supervisors from five to three) appears on all 44 styles; Kirkwood Community College Public Measure NC appears only on the 4 styles within Merged Area X."
}